title#:#Dyslexia mode
description#:#Dyslexia-friendly reading mode with OpenDyslexic font, adjusted line and letter spacing and an optional pastel background
enable#:#Enable dyslexia mode
enable_info#:#Provides an accessible reading mode with OpenDyslexic font, increased line and letter spacing and an optional pastel background.
allow_toggle#:#Student can toggle it on/off
allow_toggle_info#:#Shows a toggle button in the test player. If disabled, the mode is enforced for all participants – with no way to turn it off.
allow_customize#:#Student can adjust the appearance
allow_customize_info#:#Shows a gear button next to the toggle in the test player. Students use it to change font, background colour, line, letter and word spacing as well as the reading ruler along the same steps as below – the values chosen here then only serve as starting values. If disabled, the values set below apply unchanged.
font_label#:#Font
font_label_info#:#Replaces the test player's default font. Both fonts are designed for people with reading difficulties and ship with the module (SIL Open Font License) — nothing is loaded from outside. If adjusting is allowed, this choice acts as the starting value and students can switch.
